Betterfy "describe the sound in words" model (CLAP)
===================================================

larger_clap_music-audio-q8-1.onnx and clap-text-table.json are derived from
LAION's CLAP music checkpoint:

    music_audioset_epoch_15_esc_90.14.pt
    https://huggingface.co/lukewys/laion_clap
    sha256 fae3e9c087f2909c28a09dc31c8dfcdacbc42ba44c70e972b58c1bd1caf6dedd
    Licence: CC0-1.0 (public domain dedication)

the same weights Hugging Face publishes as laion/larger_clap_music
(Apache-2.0), whose architecture and preprocessing configuration
(revision a0b4534a14f58e20944452dff00a22a06ce629d1) are used to load them.
The Hugging Face upload's own weights are not used: its text branch is
untrained (scripts/audio-clap/clap_model.py explains).

Changes made here: the audio encoder and its projection were exported to
ONNX and their MatMul/Gemm weights quantised to int8
(scripts/audio-clap/export-audio-encoder.py); the text encoder was run once,
at build time, over the reviewed prompts in scripts/audio-clap/prompts.json
(scripts/audio-clap/build-text-table.py), and only those 512-d embeddings,
int8-packed, are shipped.

Please cite:

    Yusong Wu, Ke Chen, Tianyu Zhang, Yuchen Hui, Taylor Berg-Kirkpatrick,
    Shlomo Dubnov. "Large-scale Contrastive Language-Audio Pretraining with
    Feature Fusion and Keyword-to-Caption Augmentation." ICASSP 2023.
    arXiv:2211.06687

No warranty. The audio it hears comes from Deezer previews fetched by ISRC;
no Spotify content goes into it (docs/SMARTER-GENRES-PLAN.md §3).
